<!--
  Types IL2CPP must not strip.

  == WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ======================================================

  A WebGL build runs IL2CPP with managed stripping on. The stripper keeps what it can
  see referenced and discards the rest, and it is right almost always – the exception
  is a type whose only use is through reflection.

  JsonUtility is reflection. It walks the FIELDS of a type at runtime, and a field the
  stripper removed is a field JsonUtility cannot find. It does not throw when that
  happens: it leaves the field at its default. So a stripped wire type deserialises as
  an object full of zeros, and the game reports that the player earned nothing.

  That failure appears only in a release WebGL build. It is invisible in the editor,
  invisible in a development build, and invisible in every test – which makes it
  exactly the kind of thing worth writing down rather than discovering during a
  playtest.

  == WHY THE WHOLE ASSEMBLY AND NOT A LIST OF TYPES ============================

  Because a list is a thing somebody has to remember to add to, and the cost of being
  wrong is silent. Assembly-CSharp is the game's own code – a few hundred kilobytes of
  IL against a build measured in megabytes of engine and art – so preserving it whole
  costs approximately nothing and removes the failure mode entirely.

  The engine and package assemblies are NOT preserved here, and those are where
  stripping actually pays.
-->
<linker>

  <!--
    The game's runtime code, including every [Serializable] wire type in
    IdleExplorers.Backend and the whole shared IdleExplorers.Rules tree, which Unity
    compiles into this same assembly.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="Assembly-CSharp" preserve="all" />

  <!--
    TextMeshPro reads settings and font assets by reflection through its own
    ScriptableObject loading. Preserving the settings type specifically, rather than
    the package, because the rest of it is genuinely worth stripping.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="Unity.TextMeshPro">
    <type fullname="TMPro.TMP_Settings" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>

</linker>
